// tests/harness/lexicon-delta-033.js — the MASQUE lexicon change 0.3.2 → 0.3.3 (release 0.4.7: chart
// text and clarification prompts). Plain data only: no imports, no logic, nothing happens at import
// time. Local-only, never deployed.
//
// The second link of the lexicon delta chain: tests/harness/lexicon-delta.js stays the record of the
// approved 0.3.1 → 0.3.2 change, unchanged, and this file is applied after it. One source of truth
// for these readers:
//   tests/tools/extract-rubric.js  applies it to the 0.3.2 lexicon (applyLexiconDelta, after the 0.3.2
//                                  delta), proves it with revertLexiconDelta (and the whole chain with
//                                  revertLexiconChain), checks the lead's words, the source tag and the
//                                  basis of every row, every item and probe named, and appends
//                                  `changelog` as the rubric's last change-log entry;
//   tests/suites/values.js         proves the shipped lexicon is exactly 0.3.1 + both deltas (AD13 and
//                                  AD18), exempts only these leaves from the provenance sweep and checks
//                                  the sign-off record (lexicon033SignOffProblems);
//   tests/suites/extraction.js     audits 0.3.2 vs 0.3.3 under AD18 (block 3; block 4 for spoken lines,
//                                  since the lead's decision D9 of 2026-10-12);
//   tests/suites/capture.js, render-scribe.js  run the 0.3.2 regression checks on the 0.3.2-equivalent
//                                  lexicon (revertLexiconDelta(shipped, this delta)).
//
// THE REQUEST AND THE DECISIONS. On 2026-10-11 the user, who is the project's clinical lead, asked
// in chat for a large scrollable capture box, for chart text (a history and physical) to be read
// properly ("not pulsatile" must not flag pulsatile tinnitus), for endorsement and denial verbiage to
// trigger criteria properly, and for a section that asks the clinician to clarify unclear verbiage.
// `request` keeps the message verbatim (the history and physical it quoted is the gold set 0.4.0
// case k001 and tests/dev/hp-example.txt, verbatim). The lead then answered three questions
// (`decisions`, verbatim): a clear denial does not raise a red flag and is not listed; clarification
// prompts are answered with a click on the item's own options; new cue words and questions are drafted
// by the team from the lead's examples and the module's own wording, and the lead signs the full list
// off before anything is uploaded.
//
// SOURCES. Every clauses row and every clarify entry carries `source`: "lead" (the lead's own words
// in the request: the affirm cues endorses, reports, has, yes; the deny cues denies, no, lacks,
// doesn't have; the question "is the rhinorrhea clear or purulent?", kept verbatim and never
// re-cased), "module" (module text), "draft" (drafted by the team, awaiting the lead) or
// "lead-approved" (drafted by the team and approved by the lead: since the sign-off of 2026-10-12 every
// drafted row left is lead-approved, and none is a plain draft). The drafting record of each row stays
// in `basis` (a row drafted by the team keeps its basis starting "Draft"). The appended negation cues
// and the switches (wordStart, examItems, strictConflict, placeholderAsk, redFlagNegation) have no source
// key in the lexicon; their source is stated here (`appended[].source`) and in `basis`. redFlagNegation
// is the lead's decision of 2026-10-11 (Red flags).
//
// SIGN-OFF (2026-10-12). The clinical lead decided every row of the sign-off list (306 rows, read from
// commit cd34934) on the sign-off page and answered the 19 Part D questions and the two D8 follow-up
// questions in chat ("done, re-rest and upload 0.4.7"). `signOff` records it: the outcome of every row
// (278 approved, 18 struck, 10 the lead's own words), the struck rows with the basis they had, the lead's
// confirmation that the mask "aural" stays struck after being told its effect on the history and
// physical, the rows added at the sign-off (D7: the hedge "+/-"; D8: the deny cues "not associated
// with", "not accompanied by", "neg for", and chart red-flag phrases of rf_progressive and rf_asym), the
// clarification qualifiers the D8 answers removed, the engine rules the answers changed (D7, D8 "No gap
// markers from charts", D9: chart reading for spoken and demo lines too) and every Part D answer
// verbatim. The lead's decisions are final: struck rows are gone, approved rows are as they were.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 2 (2026-10-11). Chart reading applies to typed chart text only (engine: opts.chart), so a
// spoken or demo line reads none of these rows and extracts exactly as in release 0.4.6 (until the
// sign-off: since the lead's decision D9 of 2026-10-12 spoken and demo lines are read with them too). The round added
// draft rows only, each with a basis starting "Draft (review round 2)": clauses.redFlags (chart-register
// red-flag phrases for every flag), the sign "(+)" and the treatment-failure cues (affirm), "(-)" (deny
// and post), ": denies" and " - no" (post), report-header masks and "hay fever" (mask), five hedges,
// empty checkboxes (placeholder) and two clarify entries; it emptied examItems, changed the
// placeholderAsk text (now a notice) and removed from the safety clarify entries every qualifier that
// states the dangerous answer without raising its flag. Nothing here is approved beyond the lead's own
// words and decisions.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 3 (2026-10-11). The engine's chart rules were narrowed (signs between findings, abbreviations,
// later list items, label answers, lists under a denial, denied clarification qualifiers; see
// engine/extraction.js "Chart reading", R3). The round added draft rows only, each with a basis starting
// "Draft (review round 3)": the new list clauses.complement (for, in, about, after, since, on, none of),
// the deny cue "rather than", the breaks "other than", "besides" and "apart from", and the rf_focal phrase
// "slurred speech". Nothing here is approved beyond the lead's own words and decisions.
//
// Shape (applyLexiconDelta reads from, to, appended, fields; the rest is the record):
//   release, request {date, channel, by, text}, decisions {key: {date, question, answer, option}},
//   signOff {by, date, scope, channel, page, chat, totals, byList, struck, auralMask, added, alreadyARow,
//   removedQualifiers, engine, notPicked, partD, d8FollowUp, rows} (the lead's sign-off of 2026-10-12;
//   lexicon033SignOffProblems in tests/harness/diff.js checks it), appended [{path, phrases, source, why}],
//   fields [{path, from?, to, why}], basis {lexicon pointer: what the row rests on} (one per clauses
//   row, list entry and switch, and one per clarify entry), changelog.

