    "/clauses/placeholderAsk": "Draft: engine-neutral wording of the one placeholder notice (review round 2: a notice with a Dismiss control, no longer a question with only Skip; the module has no wording for unfilled template text). It names \"***\", the Epic wildcard, and shows for the other placeholder cues too; the card quotes the line",
    "/clauses/examItems": "Draft (review round 2): no item is captured inside an exam section (the default). r_normal and x_objective were removed: the lead's history and physical recorded r_normal from \"lids, lashes and lacrimal glands within normal limits\", and an office nasal exam line (\"Nose: no polyps.\") answered x_objective, which names endoscopy or CT; lead question in the CHANGELOG Part D",
    "/clauses/strictConflict/0": "Draft: x_purulent is a rule-out item (Discriminators, w -8): a \"yes\" lowers the index, so a chart that affirms and denies it in different words records nothing and asks (a conflict card) rather than letting the affirmed mention win",
    "/clauses/strictConflict/1": "Draft: x_objective is a rule-out item (Discriminators, w -8): a \"yes\" lowers the index, so a chart that affirms and denies it in different words records nothing and asks (a conflict card) rather than letting the affirmed mention win",
    "/clauses/strictConflict/2": "Draft: x_lowfreq is a rule-out item (Discriminators, w -8): a \"yes\" lowers the index, so a chart that affirms and denies it in different words records nothing and asks (a conflict card) rather than letting the affirmed mention win",
