    "/clauses/redFlagNegation": "The clinical lead's decision of 2026-10-11 (decisions.redFlags, \"Don't raise, no listing\"): a red flag whose every mention is denied is not raised and not listed",
    "/clarify/0": "Inventory CL-01 (rhinorrhea quality, x_purulent): the question is the clinical lead's, verbatim (request of 2026-10-11); the answers are pr_purulence's options (module: \"Yes, purulent or culture-positive\" writes x_purulent yes, \"Clear or no drainage\" writes no); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Review round 2: \"bloody\" removed from the qualifiers (bleeding is rf_mass's, not an answer to the purulence question). Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Rule-out cards stay\"): the positive-answer qualifiers purulent, thick, green, yellow, cloudy, discolored, discoloured, colored, coloured and culture removed (they state pr_purulence's \"Yes, purulent or culture-positive\"), so a stated positive that nothing captured is still asked; clear, watery and thin stay",
    "/clarify/1": "Inventory CL-02 (tinnitus quality, rf_pulsatile): question and answers are pr_tinnitus_quality's (module); triggers are v_aural phrases plus drafts, qualifiers rf_pulsatile phrases plus drafts. Review round 2: a qualifier that states the dangerous answer stays only when it is itself an rf_pulsatile phrase, so stating it raises the flag (\"pulsatile\", \"whooshing\"); \"pulsing\", \"pulses\" and \"heartbeat\" removed, so the card stays. Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Safety cards stay\"): \"clicking\" and \"steady\" removed, so a stated danger without a flag phrase still gets asked",
    "/clarify/2": "Inventory CL-03 (ear-symptom laterality, rf_asym): question and answers are pr_laterality's (module); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Review round 2: \"left\", \"right\", \"unilateral\", \"one ear\" and \"same ear\" removed (they state the dangerous answer and raised nothing), so the card stays; only the safe answers (bilateral, both ears, alternating) resolve it",
    "/clarify/3": "Inventory CL-04 (hearing-loss tempo, rf_ssnhl): question and answers are pr_sudden_drop's (module); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Review round 2: \"sudden\" removed (it states the dangerous answer; \"sudden hearing loss\" now raises rf_ssnhl through clauses.redFlags, and any other sudden wording leaves the card). Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Safety cards stay\"): \"progressive\" removed",
    "/clarify/4": "Inventory CL-05 (fluctuating hearing, x_lowfreq): question and answers are pr_audiogram's (module); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Review round 2: \"audiogram\", \"audiometry\" and \"hearing test\" removed (they name a test, not its result, so they no longer silence the card). Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Rule-out cards stay\"): the positive-answer qualifiers low-frequency and low frequency removed (they state pr_audiogram's \"Yes, it fluctuates\"), leaving no qualifier",
    "/clarify/5": "Inventory CL-06 (dizziness morphology, v_vertigo): question and answers are pr_internal_vertigo's (module; \"Yes — rocking or bobbing\" writes v_vertigo 2, \"Yes, but only seconds at a time\" writes 1); triggers are the v_vertigo cues that name no sensation; qualifiers are drafts",
    "/clarify/6": "Inventory CL-10 (ear pain, n_otalgia): question and answers are the item's (module: its ask, Yes / No); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Ear-pain card stays\"): the qualifier \"deep\" removed, so ear pain that was not captured is still asked, leaving no qualifier",
    "/clarify/7": "Inventory CL-12 (smell loss persistence, x_anosmia): question and answers are pr_smell's (module); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Rule-out cards stay\"): the positive-answer qualifiers between episodes, between flares, persistent, constant and all the time removed (they state pr_smell's \"Reduced even between flares\"); only during stays",
    "/clarify/8": "Inventory CL-13 (nasal obstruction side, rf_mass): question and answers are pr_nasal_mass's (module); triggers and qualifiers are drafts. Review round 2: \"one side\", \"one-sided\", \"unilateral\", \"left\" and \"right\" removed (they state the dangerous answer), so the card stays unless clauses.redFlags raises rf_mass",
    "/clarify/9": "Inventory CL-18 (\"HINTS negative\"): question and answers are pr_head_impulse's (module; notes only, nothing scored); triggers and qualifiers are drafts",
    "/clarify/10": "Inventory CL-19 (neck pain): question and answers are pr_neck's (module; a supporting-feature probe, unscored); triggers and qualifiers are drafts",
    "/clarify/11": "Inventory CL-20 (viral onset, n_viral): question and answers are the item's (module: its ask, Yes / No); triggers and qualifiers are drafts",
    "/clarify/12": "Draft (review round 2): a report header that names a scan or scope without its result (\"ct showed\", \"scope showed\", \"lund-mackay\", masked in chart text) asks pr_scan_detail's question with its answers (module: \"Real inflammation reported\" writes x_objective yes, \"Genuinely clear\" writes no); qualifiers are the x_objective result phrases. Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Rule-out cards stay\"): the positive-answer qualifiers scan showed inflammation, opacification, mucosal thickening and polyps removed (they state pr_scan_detail's \"Real inflammation reported\"), leaving no qualifier",
    "/clarify/13": "Draft (review round 2): a report header that names a hearing test without its result (\"audiogram showed\", \"hearing test showed\", masked in chart text) asks pr_audiogram's question with its answers (module); qualifiers are the x_lowfreq result phrases. Sign-off 2026-10-12 (D8 \"Rule-out cards stay\"): the positive-answer qualifiers low frequency loss, hearing drops during and hearing comes back removed (they state pr_audiogram's \"Yes, it fluctuates\"), leaving no qualifier",
    "/clauses/deny/13": "Draft (review round 3): a contrast that denies what follows it (\"Hearing loss, abrupt rather than gradual.\" denies the safe answer \"gradual\", so the sudden-onset card keeps asking); a list denial as the lead's \"denies\"",
